From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: YCbCr output parameter (4:4:4 and 4:2:2)

A DP to HDMI converter dock (MegaChips) keeps the monitor in SDR when
the source sends RGB with HDR metadata; an iPhone through the same dock
sends YCbCr 4:2:2 (12 bit on HDMI, ST2084) and the monitor switches to
HDR. msm.dp_ycbcr sends YCbCr at 10 bpc: 1 4:4:4 when the connector asks
for BT.2020, 2 4:4:4 always, 3 4:2:2 when the connector asks for
BT.2020, 4 4:2:2 always. The DPU converts through the CDM (BT.2020 or
BT.709, limited range; 4:2:2 in the HDMI-style pack), MISC0 signals
YCbCr 4:4:4/4:2:2 BT.709, the TU uses the 4:2:2 pixel encoding, and the
VSC SDP carries the real colorimetry when it can be sent (sink support or
msm.dp_vsc_force). msm.dp_ycbcr_yuv_bit also sets the YUV bit of
DP_CONFIGURATION_CTRL. Testing only, default off.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -227,6 +227,36 @@
 	15, 7, 13, 5, 3, 11, 1, 9, 12, 4, 14, 6, 0, 8, 2, 10
 };
 
+/* CDM output for YCbCr 4:4:4 on DP: full chroma, 10 bit (not a scanout format) */
+const struct msm_format dpu_dp_ycbcr444_fmt = {
+	.pixel_format = DRM_FORMAT_YUV444,
+	.chroma_sample = CHROMA_FULL,
+	.flags = MSM_FORMAT_FLAG_YUV | MSM_FORMAT_FLAG_DX,
+};
+
+/* Same, chroma halved horizontally: YCbCr 4:2:2 in the HDMI-style pack */
+const struct msm_format dpu_dp_ycbcr422_fmt = {
+	.pixel_format = DRM_FORMAT_YUYV,
+	.chroma_sample = CHROMA_H2V1,
+	.flags = MSM_FORMAT_FLAG_YUV | MSM_FORMAT_FLAG_DX,
+};
+
+/**
+ * dpu_encoder_dp_ycbcr444 - whether DP sends YCbCr 4:4:4 (msm.dp_ycbcr)
+ * @phys_enc: Pointer to physical encoder structure
+ */
+bool dpu_encoder_dp_ycbcr444(struct dpu_encoder_phys *phys_enc)
+{
+	struct dpu_encoder_virt *dpu_enc = to_dpu_encoder_virt(phys_enc->parent);
+	struct msm_drm_private *priv = phys_enc->parent->dev->dev_private;
+
+	if (dpu_enc->disp_info.intf_type != INTF_DP || !dpu_enc->connector)
+		return false;
+
+	return msm_dp_ycbcr444(priv->kms->dp[dpu_enc->disp_info.h_tile_instance[0]],
+			       dpu_enc->connector->state, &phys_enc->cached_mode);
+}
+
